WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.617
A skill is a folder with a SKILL.md inside:

00:00:03.617 --> 00:00:06.424
a name, a description, and instructions.

00:00:06.774 --> 00:00:09.014
It can carry scripts and reference files too.

00:00:09.364 --> 00:00:11.340
Skills follow an open standard,

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:14.271
so Claude Code and Codex read the same format.

00:00:15.671 --> 00:00:17.207
Skills load in stages.

00:00:17.557 --> 00:00:21.354
At the start, only each skill's name and description are in context.

00:00:21.704 --> 00:00:25.455
When a task matches the description, or you type its slash name,

00:00:25.455 --> 00:00:27.037
the full instructions load.

00:00:27.387 --> 00:00:31.642
Scripts and reference files load only when the instructions need them,

00:00:31.642 --> 00:00:35.046
so a long list of skills costs little until one is used.

00:00:36.446 --> 00:00:38.494
These clips were built with a video skill.

00:00:38.844 --> 00:00:41.049
It carried rules that weren't obvious:

00:00:41.049 --> 00:00:46.097
the first frame becomes the thumbnail, and text under twenty-eight pixels gets flagged.

00:00:46.447 --> 00:00:48.040
None of that was in a prompt.

00:00:48.040 --> 00:00:50.458
The skill loaded it when the task needed it.

00:00:50.808 --> 00:00:53.458
It also knew how to check and render each clip,

00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:55.544
so that part never needed explaining.

00:00:56.944 --> 00:00:58.681
The description is the trigger,

00:00:58.681 --> 00:01:01.147
so write it as "Use when" and the situation.

00:01:01.497 --> 00:01:05.593
Every description costs context on every request, so keep them short.

00:01:05.943 --> 00:01:10.103
If a personal skill and a project skill share a name, the personal one wins.

00:01:10.453 --> 00:01:13.589
When you paste the same playbook a third time, make it a skill.

00:01:13.939 --> 00:01:16.495
A long procedure can run in its own subagent,

00:01:16.495 --> 00:01:18.653
so it doesn't flood your conversation.

00:01:19.003 --> 00:01:21.723
Codex reads skills from .agents/skills,

00:01:21.723 --> 00:01:25.489
and you call one by typing a dollar sign and its name.
